data.content:
Done. Here's what changed:

**`Clock.cs`** — ambient time source using `AsyncLocal<T>` so parallel tests stay isolated. Production reads `TimeProvider.System`; cost is one null-check per call.

**`InvoiceCalculator.cs`** — now reads `Clock.UtcNow` instead of `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow`.

**Usage in tests:**

```csharp
using (Clock.Override(new DateTimeOffset(2026, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)))
{
    var calc = new InvoiceCalculator();
    Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 12, 31, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)));
}
// Clock automatically reverts when the using-block ends.
```

No DI, no NuGet packages, no constructor changes — just swap `DateTimeOffset.UtcNow` → `Clock.UtcNow` in any class that needs controllable time.
